descriptions.job-1lxamll:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a 12-week internship during summer 2027.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the Institutional Operations Solutions (IOS) team within the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers/product-groups&quot;&gt;Institutional&lt;/a&gt; group as a Finance Operations Intern. This team manages risk and delivers operational solutions across Coinbase’s Institutional organization, supporting a broad range of teams and functions that help scale the institutional business. You&#39;ll work cross-functionally with internal stakeholders and institutional clients, tackling real operational challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support day-to-day IOS operations while identifying and managing operational risk across compliance and regulatory requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve existing processes and risk management capabilities, recommending solutions backed by data analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Engineering, and other cross-functional stakeholders to build technology solutions that support institutional operations at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze data sets and deliver recommendations grounded in sound quantitative reasoning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with fellow interns on a group project solving a real business problem, presenting findings and solutions to the leadership team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a degree or certificate in business, management, finance, accounting, or a related discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated problem-solving ability with capacity to identify second-order effects and streamline processes accordingly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven willingness to engage cross-functional stakeholders and collaborate in team settings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with finance or banking concepts, with interest in crypto and digital assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Position ID: P78040&lt;/p&gt;
